              "printed_page": 870,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Can also occur in intact females or neutered individuals; marking reported in 10% of neutered males and 5% of spayed females.",
              "pdf_page": 952,
              "printed_page": 870,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Roaming and mounting may be seen in 5–10% of neutered males.",
              "pdf_page": 952,
              "printed_page": 870,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "No age or breed predilection for marking or roaming.",
              "pdf_page": 952,
              "printed_page": 870,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Mounting may be more common in sexually deprived, intact male cats mounting other males, females, kittens, people, and inanimate objects.",
              "pdf_page": 952,
              "printed_page": 870,
              "column": 1
            }
          ]
        },
        "SIGNS": {
          "present": true,
          "status": "content",
          "source_heading": "SIGNS",
          "canonical_heading": "SIGNS",
          "content_blocks": [
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Urine marking—characterized by the cat backing up to vertical object with an erect and quivering tail and projecting a stream of urine backward; may also occur with the cat assuming a squatting posture and depositing urine on horizontal surfaces, notably personal or novel items in the environment; urine deposited on multiple surface types in conjunction with normal litter box use for toileting of urine and feces.",
              "pdf_page": 952,
              "printed_page": 870,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Mounting—of other cats, people, or objects.",
              "pdf_page": 952,
              "printed_page": 870,
              "column": 1
            }
          ]
        },
